      "message": "bind_f \u003c\u003c device is buffered — the real write to sysfs (and any bind error) only happens when the stream flushes at function exit, after the \"bound\" success line. So the fail() check runs before the write lands and never catches a failed bind. A \u003c\u003c std::flush before the check would fix it.",
